# store deploy — copy to .env. TLS is terminated by the deployment environment.
#
# NOTE: nothing here configures the CONNECTOR any more. Since the cutover to the
# Rust connector (connector#755) there is no environment-variable layer on that
# side at all — every connector value comes from ./connector.toml, and its two
# secrets are FILES you generate next to it (see README.md). What remains below
# configures the store app, the image pins, and the published port.

# ── Identities ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED: store Nostr identity. Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
STORE_NOSTR_SECRET_KEY=
#
# The connector's identities are NOT here. `TOON_MNEMONIC` used to derive the
# settlement key at boot and no longer does anything:
#   deploy/signer.key      — fresh random, this node's ILP identity, holds no money
#   deploy/settlement.key  — derived at NIP-06 m/44'/1237'/0'/0/0, spends value
# Both are gitignored and mounted read-only into the container.
#
# The old note here said this identity also funded the store box's own
# kind:10032 self-announce. It does not: the always-on `selfAnnounce` timer is
# gone for good, and this settlement key isn't wired to any replacement — the
# Rust connector's `[announce]` section + one-shot `connector announce` verb
# exist on this bundle's pinned tag, but `connector.toml` doesn't configure
# them. See README.md.

# ── Arweave wallet ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# base64(JSON RSA JWK) of a funded Arweave wallet. Empty → ephemeral free-tier
# (≤100KB uploads, no deposit; the ephemeral key rotates on every restart).
STORE_ARWEAVE_JWK_B64=
# Flat per-job fee (base units). Informational only — the connector enforces the
# flat route price in connector.toml, which is what a payer is actually charged.
FEE_PER_JOB=10

# ── Images ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The connector image baked into store-connector, but ONLY when you build it
# yourself (`docker compose up --build`). On the production path — pull
# STORE_CONNECTOR_IMAGE, `up` without --build — this variable does NOTHING: no
# environment variable can change what is already baked into a pulled image,
# and what is baked in is deploy/Dockerfile's own ARG default at the commit CI
# built. To adopt a newer connector there, bump that ARG default and cut a new
# store-connector release; bumping this line alone will not do it.
#
# Pin an exact `rust-sha-` tag, never the floating `rust-main`: the config
# parser is `deny_unknown_fields` and startup is fail-closed, so a schema
# drift is a refuse-to-start.
#
# The `connector` package holds BOTH lineages under one name. A plain semver tag
# (`3.28.0`, `latest`) is the RETIRED TypeScript node, which reads YAML and will
# not start on ./connector.toml. Only `rust-*` tags are this connector.
CONNECTOR_TAG=rust-sha-440eab7
# The published store-connector image (prod: pin a tag and `up` without --build).
STORE_CONNECTOR_IMAGE=ghcr.io/toon-protocol/store-connector:latest
# The published store app image.
STORE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/toon-protocol/store:latest

# ── Optional jobs (kind:5095 ArNS buy, kind:5096/5098 gas stations) ───────────
# All OPTIONAL and OFF by default (empty = disabled) — see entrypoint-store.ts's
# env-mapping doc comment for full validation rules. Setting one of these here
# is the ONLY edit needed to enable its job; docker-compose.yml already passes
# all of them through, so there is no second "uncomment this line" step.
#
# 128-char hex (64-byte Ed25519 keypair). Enables kind:5095 ArNS brokered buy.
ARNS_DVM_SOLANA_SECRET_KEY=
# devnet (default) | mainnet. Shared by the kind:5095/5096 jobs; mainnet is
# explicit opt-in.
ARNS_NETWORK=devnet
# 128-char hex, MUST differ from ARNS_DVM_SOLANA_SECRET_KEY (toon-meta#163
# mitigation a — the store refuses to boot with the same key in both). Enables
# kind:5096 Solana gas-station co-sign/broadcast.
GAS_STATION_SOLANA_SECRET_KEY=
# base58 Solana program id of the TOON payment-channel program for the
# configured ARNS_NETWORK cluster (issue #67) — take this from this box's own
# live kind:10032 announce, not a preset. Absent: channel-program jobs stay
# unsupported, same as before this variable existed.
GAS_STATION_CHANNEL_PROGRAM_ID=
# JSON array of EVM chain configs for kind:5098 evm-gas-station (issue #68):
# [{chainId, rpcUrl, forwarderAddress, tokenNetworkAddress, relayerPrivateKey}]
# One dedicated per-chain relayer wallet per entry. Malformed throws at boot.
EVM_GAS_STATION_CONFIG_JSON=
# Overrides the default 120s EVM quote deadline.
EVM_GAS_STATION_QUOTE_TTL_MS=
# Overrides the default 300_000 gas cap per forwarded call.
EVM_GAS_STATION_MAX_GAS=

# ── Ports ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ Docker's `ports:` publish bypasses ufw — see docker-compose.yml's header
# warning. EDGE_BIND keeps the paid edge on loopback, reachable only through
# this box's own reverse proxy / TLS terminator; change it only if that proxy
# runs somewhere other than the same host.
EDGE_BIND=127.0.0.1
EDGE_PORT=3000
